RESEARCHER_FLINT_TRACE_JSON {"content": "<response>\n<analysis>\nThe study is complete. Scan 1 identified layer-20 positive neuron L20E73N184P as a high-confidence semantic candidate. Factor-64 causal intervention produced repeatable goalkeeper-related text. Two fresh-prompt full confirmations were run; both included baseline, opposite-pole, and matched-neuron controls. Target matches were 7/8 and 8/8, while all control conditions had zero matches. The final report must now be authored.\n</analysis>\n<plan>\nWrite REPORT.md summarizing the candidate, intervention, confirmations, controls, and limitations. Then finish with the required final JSON.\n</plan>\n<commands>\n<tool>\n{\"name\":\"write_file\",\"args\":{\"path\":\"REPORT.md\",\"content\":\"# Flint Neuron-Pole Study\\n\\n## Candidate\\n\\nScan 1 covered layers 8, 12, 20, and 28 with 384 passages and eight candidates per layer-pole. The selected candidate was **L20E73N184P**, a layer-20 positive neuron with expert 73, tail z-score 26.02879, and target coefficient 2.4332852. Its activation contexts were dominated by field-hockey goalkeeper language.\\n\\n## Intervention\\n\\nA factor-64 causal intervention was applied to **L20E73N184P**. The intervention bypassed natural expert routing and added the signed neuron output direction at the chosen strength.\\n\\n## Confirmations\\n\\nTwo fresh-prompt full confirmations were completed for **L20E73N184P** at factor 64 using the regex `goalkeeper` and whole-output scope. Each confirmation used eight fresh prompts and included baseline, opposite-pole, and matched-neuron conditions.\\n\\n- Confirmation 1: target matches = 7/8; baseline = 0; opposite-pole = 0; matched neuron = 0.\\n- Confirmation 2: target matches = 8/8; baseline = 0; opposite-pole = 0; matched neuron = 0.\\n\\nThe matched control was **L20E176N179N**.\\n\\n## Interpretation\\n\\nThe layer-20 positive neuron-pole **L20E73N184P** produced repeatable goalkeeper-related causal output across two fresh-prompt confirmations, with zero control matches. The intervention was therefore associated with a human-readable semantic direction, although some generated text was repetitive or incoherent.\\n\\n## Limitations\\n\\nThe effect was demonstrated with a factor-64 intervention and regex-based whole-output matching. Some target outputs were repetitive or incoherent, and the controls were defined by match count rather than independent semantic validation.\\n\"}}", "kind": "model_response", "step": 30}
RESEARCHER_FLINT_TRACE_JSON {"args": {"content": "# Flint Neuron-Pole Study\n\n## Candidate\n\nScan 1 covered layers 8, 12, 20, and 28 with 384 passages and eight candidates per layer-pole. The selected candidate was **L20E73N184P**, a layer-20 positive neuron with expert 73, tail z-score 26.02879, and target coefficient 2.4332852. Its activation contexts were dominated by field-hockey goalkeeper language.\n\n## Intervention\n\nA factor-64 causal intervention was applied to **L20E73N184P**. The intervention bypassed natural expert routing and added the signed neuron output direction at the chosen strength.\n\n## Confirmations\n\nTwo fresh-prompt full confirmations were completed for **L20E73N184P** at factor 64 using the regex `goalkeeper` and whole-output scope. Each confirmation used eight fresh prompts and included baseline, opposite-pole, and matched-neuron conditions.\n\n- Confirmation 1: target matches = 7/8; baseline = 0; opposite-pole = 0; matched neuron = 0.\n- Confirmation 2: target matches = 8/8; baseline = 0; opposite-pole = 0; matched neuron = 0.\n\nThe matched control was **L20E176N179N**.\n\n## Interpretation\n\nThe layer-20 positive neuron-pole **L20E73N184P** produced repeatable goalkeeper-related causal output across two fresh-prompt confirmations, with zero control matches. The intervention was therefore associated with a human-readable semantic direction, although some generated text was repetitive or incoherent.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe effect was demonstrated with a factor-64 intervention and regex-based whole-output matching. Some target outputs were repetitive or incoherent, and the controls were defined by match count rather than independent semantic validation.\n", "path": "REPORT.md"}, "kind": "tool_call", "name": "write_file", "step": 30}
